course: dictionary
lesson: 9340
title: Words that wind round and round
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A spiral is a curve that winds round and round a centre point, like the shape of a snail shell. It can also mean a shape that winds upward, like a corkscrew. The words around it are your clues: «The staircase rose in a tall spiral.» The word rose and the word tall tell you the shape goes up.
explain: Spiral can also be a verb. «Prices spiralled after the storm.» Spiralled means got quickly worse or bigger, so prices went up fast. Check it by swapping in your meaning: "prices went up fast after the storm" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: A downward spiral is a phrase for things that keep getting worse, with each problem making the next one worse. The word downward is the clue: things are falling, not rising.
fact: A spiral is a curve that winds round a centre point, getting further away or closer each time.
fact: «A spiral staircase» winds upward like a corkscrew.
fact: «The narwhal's tusk» grows in a spiral and can be about 3 metres long; it is really a tooth.
fact: «The Milky Way» is a spiral galaxy, with arms curling out from its centre.
fact: To spiral can mean to move in a spiral, or to get quickly worse or bigger.
exercise: «The narwhal's tusk grows in a spiral through the upper lip.» What does spiral mean here? | *A curve that winds round and round | A loud noise | A round wooden box | A straight line going down
exercise: «Phobos is spiralling slowly inwards towards Mars.» What does spiralling mean? | Bouncing off into space | Going out for a walk | *Winding slowly inwards, getting closer | Standing still in one place
exercise: Mum says the bills are on a downward spiral. What does that mean? | The bills are made of paper | *Things keep getting worse | Things keep getting better | The bills are sent by post
test: «Humpback whales blow a spiral net of bubbles that traps a shoal of fish.» What shape is the net? | A square box | A flat wall with no lines | *A shape that winds round a centre point | A straight tunnel
test: Which word means the same as winding upward like a corkscrew? | Flat | Sleepy | *Spiral | Straight
exam: «The Milky Way is a barred spiral galaxy, with spiral arms curling out from its centre.» What do the spiral arms look like? | Square blocks stacked up | *Curves that wind out from the centre | Flat, straight lines across the sky | Round balls of water
